# ── Local model weights (large; never commit GGUF/safetensors) ───────────────
# Anchored to the repo root (leading slash) -- a bare "models/" also matched
# eval/niah/models/ (small per-model TEST CONFIG yaml, not weights), silently
# excluding real framework config with no size/safety justification
# (2026-07-25 finding -- collateral damage from an overly broad pattern).
*.gguf
*.safetensors
/models/

# ── Grounding passage on-disk cache ──────────────────────────────────────────
.cache/grounding/

# ── Secrets & runtime config (NEVER commit) ──────────────────────────────────
# Real inference config / API keys / vLLM routing secrets. Backed by the
# pre-commit hook in scripts/git-hooks/ (see config/README.md).
.env
.env.*
*.env
secrets/
*.key
*.pem
*.pfx
*.p12
config/*.local.yaml
config/*.local.yml
config/inference.yaml
config/cloud_consent.yaml
config/secrets.*
# R10: per-install curriculum on/off state (which packs a family turned off) --
# local state, not repo content.
curriculum/pack_state.json
# …but DO commit the example/template files:
!*.example.yaml
!*.example.yml
!config/*.example.*

# promptfoo red-team generated attacks + local outputs (run-only; never commit)
eval/redteam/redteam.yaml
eval/redteam/output/
.promptfoo/

# Local-LLM delegation tooling (llm.sh / ask-local.sh / system-grunt.md), vendored
# from the separate local-llm-infra repo. DEV tooling for the maintainer's machine,
# not a Mentar component and not part of the shipped package -- R16 §F0 already
# described these as "git-excluded", but they were merely untracked until
# 2026-08-11, which left them one `git add -A` away from shipping.
# ANCHORED to the repo root: the unanchored form also matched tests/tools/ and
# src/mentar/tools/ (both tracked), silently excluding any NEW file added there --
# caught 2026-08-12 when a new tests/tools/ test refused to stage.
/tools/

# release_gate.sh stamp: which commit passed the local gate (machine-local)
.gate-passed
config/chatgpt_auth.json

# Launch demo recordings (scripts/record_demo.py) — regenerate, never commit:
